---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About · Sarvakali" sequence="devotionQuiet" description="About Sarvakali: the person and the path behind the institute.">
  <article class="page">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="kicker" data-hero>About</p>
      <h1 class="display-l" data-hero data-split>The person behind Sarvakali</h1>
      <p class="lede" data-hero>Who you will be speaking with, where the path began, and how the work is held.</p>
      <p class="proto-flag" data-hero>Placeholder page: every line in brackets is to be written with Sarvakali.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="about-grid">
      <figure class="about-portrait" data-fade>
        <div class="about-frame">
          <svg viewBox="-90 -125 180 250" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M0 -100 Q74 0 0 100 Q-74 0 0 -100Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
            <circle r="20" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <figcaption>A portrait or a photograph of the altar goes here. It could open into depth like the <a href="/depth">AI depth demo</a>.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="prose" data-fade>
        <h2>The path</h2>
        <p>[Sarvakali's story: how the path began, the teachers and moments that shaped it, and how Kali came in.]</p>
        <h2>Lineage and training</h2>
        <p>[Traditions, initiations and teachers. Training and qualifications, for example in Reiki, hypnotherapy, CBT, NLP and EFT.]</p>
        <h2>How Sarvakali works</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Every conversation begins with listening. You share as much or as little as you like.</li>
          <li>Sessions are online, over Google Meet, at a time you agree together.</li>
          <li>You never have to explain your situation in a form.</li>
          <li>Fees are discussed directly, and paid by UPI against an invoice.</li>
          <li>[Anything else Sarvakali wants every new person to know.]</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Who it is for</h2>
        <p>People of every background, faith and identity, including queer and trans people, who will always be met with respect. [Sarvakali's own words here.]</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-solid" href="/connect">Request a conversation</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/care">Boundaries and care</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
